#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:738
msgid ""
"Is used to combine the result-set of two or more SELECT statements. It "
"will return only the unique results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:742
msgid ""
"For correct work with DBMS (such as MSSQL and Oracle) queries are wrapped"
" in ``SELECT * FROM ( ... ) alias`` The main query will always have an "
"alias of ``uwrp0``. Each subsequent query added via ``union()`` will have"
" an alias ``uwrpN+1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:746
msgid ""
"All union queries will be added after the main query, regardless of the "
"order in which the ``union()`` method was called. That is, the "
"``limit()`` or ``orderBy()`` methods will be relative to the main query, "
"even if called after ``union()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:750
msgid ""
"In some cases, it may be necessary, for example, to sort or limit the "
"number of records of the query result. The solution is to use the wrapper"
" created via ``$db->newQuery()``. In the example below, we get the first "
"5 users + the last 5 users and sort the result by id:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:757
msgid "$builder->unionAll()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/database/query_builder.rst:759
msgid ""
"The behavior is the same as the ``union()`` method. However, all results "
"will be returned, not just the unique ones."
msgstr ""

